---

## Conclusion

This project successfully applied three machine learning algorithms to classify campus noise measurements into Quiet, Moderate, and Loud categories.

The Decision Tree achieved the best overall accuracy at **75.46%**, while Random Forest and Logistic Regression demonstrated better recall for Loud measurements.

The comparison highlights the importance of evaluating both overall model performance and individual classification categories.
